<%#
  THE RECORD-PAGE SKELETON -- facelift 2/4 (issue #94).

  One shape for every record page, adapted from a reference app's entity page:
  BREADCRUMB -> GRADIENT HEADING -> BADGE/META ROW -> alias/muted line, and then
  the page's own content under uppercase `h3` micro-headings (record_section).

  The ORDER lives HERE and nowhere else. A view passes the CONTENT for each part;
  it does not re-decide what comes first.

    .crumb         the trail, oldest first, with the record's own id LAST, mono
    h1             the record's name -- the gradient word on every record page
    .record-meta   the state badge(s) + the machine values (ids, dates) in mono
    .record-alias  the muted sub-line: the record's other name, or its note

  A part with nothing to say renders an EM-DASH rather than disappearing, which
  is the kb's own convention and the reason the rhythm survives a record with no
  runner, no date or no second name. The dash is a `.chip.miss` -- the studio's
  phase-1 (#93) convention for "absent, and that is intentional", not broken.

  What is deliberately NOT in here: each page's own CONTROLS (Run Job / Compose,
  Ask Jev / manifest, Refresh / back, the run-summary tiles). Those are the
  page's content, they carry page-local grid placement and page-local geometry
  classes that other pages share, and the skeleton's list does not include them.
  They render in their existing `.page-head` wrappers directly below this
  partial, which is the one position the skeleton does not have to decide.

  Locals
    crumbs      [[label, path], ...] -- the trail ABOVE the record; may be []
    crumb_id    the record's own id/name (the crumb's terminal node, mono)
    title       the record's name (rendered in the gradient)
    badges      HTML for the meta row's badges; nil -> an em-dash
    meta        the mono machine values (id, runner, dates); nil -> an em-dash
    alias_line  the muted sub-line; nil -> an em-dash
%>
<header class="record-head">
  <nav class="crumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <% Array(crumbs).each do |label, path| %>
      <%= link_to label, path %><span class="crumb-sep" aria-hidden="true">/</span>
    <% end %>
    <span class="id"><%= crumb_id %></span>
  </nav>

  <h1 class="section-title record-title"><span class="gradient-text"><%= title %></span></h1>

  <div class="record-meta">
    <% if badges.present? %>
      <%= badges %>
    <% else %>
      <span class="chip miss" aria-hidden="true">&mdash;</span>
    <% end %>
    <span class="id"><%= meta.presence || "—" %></span>
  </div>

  <p class="record-alias"><%= alias_line.presence || "—" %></p>
</header>
